{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals","id":87281,"title":"I'm Not Getting Abyssals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-08T23:25:31-08:00","id":87281,"title":"I'm Not Getting Abyssals","content":"Been thinking a lot about 3rd editions take of Exalts lately, namely Infernals. Now that pretty much everything I hated about them is being removed and the devs are abandoning the Reclamation/Infernals 2.0 concept, I'm really looking forward to using them. Even with what little we have to go on, I already have several ideas for Infernal characters villainous, heroic, and everything in between. <br /> <br /> Every time I look at Abyssals though, the only thing I can think is &quot;why are the hell are you guys still around?&quot; Yeah, I know Abyssals are the classic foils to the Solars and they have different themes an' all, but looking at the two previews, it's hard not to notice the overlap between Infernals and Abyssals. To be frank, Infernals make better foils to Solars than Abyssals. A vision of a corrupt, decadent First Age Solar recklessly weilding the power of the capacious mad Titans they once warred against is far more of a compelling image than an undead demi-god that channels the power of thirteen pissy Solar ghosts who in turn serve the Neverborn. It certainly doesn't help that Abyssals have traditionally protrayed as murderbots constantly being screwed over by Resonance. <br /> <br /> Now I'll go ahead and admit that I have a bias in that I've always preferred Deathlords as being powerful ghosts who rule over kingdoms of the dead and not a little over a dozen ghosts of First Age Solars, so there's that. I think part of my problem is how the Underworld and Neverborn have been presented in editions past. There are good bits to both, yes, but on a whole, what should have been interesting instead became boring and inconsistent at best. The Abyssal preview did a little to alleviate my concerns, but I'm still not really sold on Abyssals. Is there something about Abyssals I'm missing or not understanding here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:30:59-08:00","id":87284,"title":"","content":"It's really too early to be making a call. Abyssals are at least two years off. Possibly more. Very little about them has been hammered down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:47:44-08:00","id":87322,"title":"","content":"I'm expecting the underworld to be extensively rewritten, the Devs seem to feel it's very dull (and for the most part, I think they're correct), and I wouldn't be surprised if the Deathlords and Neverborn are rewritten. One of the Devs said something about reducing the role of Oblivion itself, which is likely to increase the role of the Neverborn and Deathlords, so that would probably necessitate a rewrite.<br /> And all of that is likely to bleed into Abyssals.<br /> <br /> But as Saur Ops Specialist says, it's a long way away... I'm sure some info on the Deathlords and Neverborn will be in the Core, so we'll see how that goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T01:02:29-08:00","id":87332,"title":"","content":"They're planning to basically rework each of the Deathlords into a different character with different goals and ambitions, instead of 13 distinct flavours of Skeletor.<br /> Like, this is what Mr Morke has said about the Walker in Darkness:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">What I have for the Walker atm, is that he marches his spectral army around Creation, and his Shadowland marches with him, like a dark cloud moving over the landscape. He offers his military services to embattled nations for a grim price.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Still very philosophical. I love the idea of him kneeling in a courtroom, accepting an honor from a king, while the queen is backed up in her throne as far as she can get, the whole court is aghast and terrified, and swimming with living shadows, an he is holding a bleeding rose up to the queen in offering.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Oh, I always planned him to remain a warrior poet. The mercenary angle is to make him more accessible, a character that kings and leaders have actually treated with.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The question is always whether you can pay the Walker's price. It's a bit of a monkey's paw.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:04:56-07:00","id":87407,"title":"","content":"Maybe because you only look at the their &quot;foil of Solar&quot;, &quot;Corrupted Solar&quot; which only ever come up in forum discussion and not on table instead of looking at their charm which make people decide whether they want to play Abyssal or not.<br /> <br /> Exalted need a splat for people who like death-related power/aesthetic and Abyssal are their choice since chosen of Ending really can't go around with skull-armor (not to mention death is just one of their purview) and Yozi generally stay away from deathy-deathly-dead-death stuff as far as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 03-09-2014, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:23:17-07:00","id":87413,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of the exact opposite of you. Now that most everything I like about Infernals is being taken away, I'm starting to wonder if Abyssals (my most hated Exalt type) might start being more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:29:47-07:00","id":87419,"title":"","content":"That's a very, very different conception of Walker. I'm... not sure if I like it. I don't like the mercenary bit, seems kind of low for a Deathlord. I like the warrior poet bit though. But honestly, old Walker was definitely the least nuanced of the Deathlords, so it's a lot better than &quot;I want to kill everyone, I hate MoW, I have amnesia and a dark secret I don't know (I used to bone MoW), also I'm stupid regarding Abyssal castes&quot;.<br /> Though I was amused by his pet doggy.<br /> <br /> It would suggest at least some of the other Deathlords are having big rewrites too, as that's fairly fundamental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:50:22-07:00","id":87425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Two-Shadows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals#post87281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but looking at the two previews, it's hard not to notice the overlap between Infernals and Abyssals. To be frank, Infernals make better foils to Solars than Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see them as incorporating two different, but related, functions.<br /> My view of Abyssals is that of the anti-thesis to Solars. Like some kind of karmic force of balance to the 'Good' of Solars entry into creation (even though this karmic balancework took <i>some</i> time, but it's what's going on now that matters from this point of view ^^ <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). This is especially hightened by the choice of word/names for each type*<br /> <br /> But infernals, to me, harken back to the First Age Solars, with all their excentricities unleashed. Now powered even more by being brought to light (and probably encouraged by their &quot;blessers&quot;).<br /> So while Abyssals serve as direct opposition, and thereby define Solars as what they are not, I view Infernals as the looming reminder, and threat, of what they may yet become.<br /> <br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;Solar&quot; does not mean simply &quot;of the Sun&quot;, but is in creation what the word &quot;stellar&quot; is in our world (&quot;stellar&quot; meaning something along the lines of &quot;at the height of the stars&quot;, i.e: as high as you can rise. Since the sun is at the top in Creation &quot;Solar&quot; instead fills the spot of being &quot;at the highest height&quot;.) While an abyss is still an abyss. that is to say, &quot;Abyssal&quot; means something along the lines of &quot;the lowest depth&quot;. Understood within this is a definition of the value of height as being; high = good, low = bad. solar = the ultimate height to which a wo/man can rise. abyssal = the lowest depth to which a wo/man can sink.<br /> Ofcourse this is not to say that a Solar has to be a good person. And in the same way an Abyssal does not have to be an evil or bad person. But generally speaking, it is, more than just a fight between individuals, a clash between two metaphysical, oppositional forces. This is all in my personal interpretation, note.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:05:15-07:00","id":87430,"title":"","content":"Abyssals as anti-Solars sounded like a good idea, but I don't think it worked well in 2nd ed. I think in this edition the developers want to move more away from them being anti-Solars, and more towards their own thing. Obviously they'll still have lots of opposing themes (Solars have light, Abyssals have darkness, etc).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, with their themes of &quot;decadence and casual power&quot; I think the Devs want to move Infernals more towards what you are talking about. Not necessarily because they want them to be the Solars of the Old Realm, just coincidentally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:46:02-07:00","id":87443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87430#post87430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals as anti-Solars sounded like a good idea, but I don't think it worked well in 2nd ed. I think in this edition the developers want to move more away from them being anti-Solars, and more towards their own thing. Obviously they'll still have lots of opposing themes (Solars have light, Abyssals have darkness, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... consider these from John:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Throwing out the castes might as well be throwing out the book. &quot;Dark Solars&quot; continues to be a concept that fires my imagination, far more than &quot;Exalt of [Oblivion/the Void/other generic concept]&quot; ever will, and that the game has pushed them in that direction in 2e is one of the number one reasons why they went from arguably the most popular splat in 1e to the hands-down least popular splat in 2e. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that I cannot escape a comparison to Solars because it is essentially a Solar Charm set, so I am not proceeding from a direct comparison and I am rather building toward apexes that reflect the Deathlords rather than the Unconquered Sun. Broadness may not come of one Charm, but I'm still just feeling my muscles, you know? Seeing what I can do. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order to preserve their castes and castemarks, they will still have a core set based on the Solar paradigm of raising abilities and exuding excellence and skill. But I am trying to turn away from the myth-hero to the dead-hero, which I am having to somewhat make up as I go. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:55:38-07:00","id":87445,"title":"","content":"Eh, fair enough, that's not the impression I'd got previously.<br /> I only came back to this forum a few days ago, so I've missed some developer quotes.<br /> <br /> I actually don't like the idea of Deathlord charms, it's a bit too like the Yozi charms of 2nd ed, which initially seemed like a great idea to me, but had some problems. But saying that, the Lover charm-tree he posted seemed fairly decent (though of course it was all about social-fu in a social-fu system we haven't seen, so slightly difficult to judge, but the themes seemed fine, which isn't easy in a charm-tree about seduction, that tends to set people off).<br /> It probably depends somewhat on how he and the other Devs write the Deathlords. If they write the Deathlords in such a way as to ensure it makes sense for Abyssals to have all the cool charms they want them to have, that might be okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T06:54:31-07:00","id":87457,"title":"","content":"The Solars have returned to Creation as a blank slate and carry with them the hope of Creation's future. Theirs is a struggle to resist the temptations that corrupted their predecessors. <br /> <br /> The Infernals emphasize the excesses and debauchery of the First Age Solars who used their powers for selfish ends. Theirs is a struggle to learn to use their powers for the sake of others rather than petty indulgence. <br /> <br /> The Abyssals emphasize the callousness of the First Age Solars who turned their powers against Creation instead of protecting it. Theirs is a struggle to learn to use their powers to protect rather than destroy. <br /> <br /> Or they can all fail and doom the world again. Their choice. <br /> <br /> In any case, the Abyssal narrative is a positive one; it seeks to <i>achieve</i> something rather than to <i>avoid</i> something. The Abyssals who are doomed are those who choose to use their power solely for the sake of destruction. The Abyssals who are on the path to salvation are those who learn to connect with something and use their powers to protect it. It could be anything from their Deathlord liege to their undead followers, as long as they're trying to preserve it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:34:46-07:00","id":87472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87445#post87445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, fair enough, that's not the impression I'd got previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>In retrospect, I was perhaps reading too much into the fact that they're dumping the Mirror charm set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssals who are on the path to salvation are those who learn to connect with something and use their powers to protect it. It could be anything from their Deathlord liege to their undead followers, as long as they're trying to preserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I'm quite happy with good Abyssals being anti-heroes who use their death powers for good by slaying the wicked. Destruction could be good if you use it destroy evil. Or just destroying things to create a slate for new things to be created.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking of Shiva in his role of Destruction, or in all the art where he's depicted slaying demons, as a good inspiration for a non-evil Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:41:26-07:00","id":87475,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'd definitely count killing bad people as protecting something so long as they're deliberately killing bad people in order to prevent them from doing bad things, rather than just randomly killing people who happen to do bad things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:53:01-07:00","id":87479,"title":"","content":"Sure, fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T10:41:25-07:00","id":87573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87407#post87407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted need a splat for people who like death-related power/aesthetic and Abyssal are their choice since chosen of Ending really can't go around with skull-armor (not to mention death is just one of their purview) and Yozi generally stay away from deathy-deathly-dead-death stuff as far as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want an Exalt who revolves around &quot;death&quot; without being cast as a Dark Solar, you may have your answer in the Liminals.<br /> <br /> We don't know much about them yet, but they're born of failed attempts to raise the dead, and spend a lot of time in the Underworld. We know that the devs think they add depth both to the Underworld and to the Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:16:03-07:00","id":87647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87573#post87573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want an Exalt who revolves around &quot;death&quot; without being cast as a Dark Solar, you may have your answer in the Liminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't really go about in skull-covered armour either, though. They're subtler than that.<br /> Their Charms will probably be in the right ballpark, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 03-09-2014, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:21:18-07:00","id":87652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87647#post87647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't really go about in skull-covered armour either, though. They're subtler than that.<br /> Their will probably be in the right ballpark, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>One set of powers the Liminals won't likely have, however, are powers that draw on being like a corpse, or like the dead. That seems to be for the Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:32:24-07:00","id":87658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87652#post87652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One set of powers the Liminals won't likely have, however, are powers that draw on being like a corpse, or like the dead. That seems to be for the Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that many Liminals used to be corpses, I don't really imagine that being vetoed as creative space for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:50:43-07:00","id":87671,"title":"","content":"&quot;Being like a corpse&quot; is like their version of knowing what the time is.<br /> Seriously, they <i>can't be killed</i> except by fire and massive brain trauma, both of which are recurring zombie weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:51:16-07:00","id":87672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87658#post87658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that many Liminals used to be corpses, I don't really imagine that being vetoed as creative space for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. I was working off Holden's answer below, but I could well have misinterpreted:<br /> <br /> <i>Hecaton: [W]ould it be okay to assume a charm that, say, let a character ignore pain because corpses just don't give a fuck might be workable for both Abyssals and Liminals?<br /> Holden: Wouldn't be very Liminal-appropriate because they're pointed in the other direction. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:55:34-07:00","id":87673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87647#post87647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They don't really go about in skull-covered armour either, though. They're subtler than that. Their will probably be in the right ballpark, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Liminal can wear skull-covered armor if you want!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:08:41-07:00","id":87684,"title":"","content":"That doesn't mean it's the default look, though. Scarification feels more appropriate for a garish Liminal, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 03-09-2014, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:28:30-07:00","id":87696,"title":"","content":"Alright, so, Infernals and Abyssals.<br /> <br /> The thing to remember about the Solars is that they committed two great collective sins, and the Abyssals and Infernals represent the Solars at these moments of shame, horror and weakness.<br /> <br /> The Abyssals represent the first sin, the Slaying of the Primordials during the Primordial War. Yeah, it was a great thing for the gods and humanity, but it was also a fundamentally selfish and destructive act that broke the very metaphysics of Creation. The Exalted are <i>murderers</i> dressed up in shiny clothing, <i>war criminals</i> bearing medals and honors that mock the victims of their atrocities. The Abyssal Exalted are the embodiments of this truth, the Solar Exaltation as it &quot;really&quot; is: black with sin, stained by the blood of the Primordials and an affront to all that is natural. They are the Exalted as the Neverborn see them, and guided by the Deathlords, the deathknights become the instruments of their vengeance.<br /> <br /> The Infernals represent the second sin, the decadence of the First Age. The Solars had always had their vices, but generally their efforts had led to good more than evil. However, as time went on and their enemies started to disappear, they became more and more decadent, indulgent, and jaded. Less and less did they feel like humans who had rose higher, and more and more did they feel as though they were... above humanity. Above the restraints of mortal flesh. Above even things like good and evil. And like in Animal Farm, when they could no longer tell the difference between the pigs and the humans, no more could they tell the difference between the Solars and the Primordials they had cast down. Fitting, then, that some of their souls would become channels for the might of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> If you need a more concrete sort of difference, imagine their general attitudes: Infernals tend more towards Kubla Khan with his Xanadu and Caligula with his ridiculous orgies and gladiator matches (or, for a slightly more ridiculous image, Scrooge McDuck swimming in a giant pile of gold coins). Abyssals tend more towards a character in a Frank Miller comic, or maybe Neil Gaiman's Sandman (especially Death and Destiny).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":283,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","user":"MrInsecure","date":". 03-09-2014, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T13:48:39-07:00","id":87709,"title":"","content":"Setting aside historical issues (they can't really <i>remove </i>Abyssals now, they were originally added in part as an oWoD reference), Abyssals are there because they fill a niche that is not filled by infernals, liminals or ghosts. They're goth and undead-themed in a way that Infernals don't serve, they draw more on the undead-as-stylish-and-awesome thematics than Liminals (Kindred to the Liminals' Prometheans, if you will), and they let you play in any sandbox, unlike ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:05:27-07:00","id":87761,"title":"","content":"I think the big difference between the Exalted as what kind of story they normally tell:<br /> <br /> A Solar story is a legend, full of impressive feats and grand deeds.<br /> <br /> A Lunar story is a disaster movie, something happens and people simply have to deal with it. Barbarians invade, Godzilla attacks Tokyo, whatever.<br /> <br /> A Sidereal story is a myth/heist story, they use various mythic tropes to enact a carefully planned course of action.<br /> <br /> An Abyssal story is a ghost story, the actions of someone come to light and people have to deal with it or be destroyed.<br /> <br /> An Infernal story is all about the villain protagonist, where the point is in celebrating the actions of a scoundrel. (There has got to be a better name for stories like the Wolf of Wallstreet or Faust).<br /> <br /> An Alchemical story is a superhero comic, a great person fighting for their cultural values.<br /> <br /> A Fair Folk story is fan-fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2481-lordofarcana","name":"LordofArcana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:14:13-07:00","id":88221,"title":"","content":"Here's one difference: Infernals draw from fear of the past. Abyssals draw more from fear of the future.<br /> <br /> No, really. Abyssals are in large part about a future that'll be worse than the present. They draw on the cycle of Creation switching to diminished rulership over and over - the Primordials, Solar, Dragon-Blooded, and the old hints that it'd become the World of Darkness. That's part of why they have European aesthetics - to evoke latter-day imperialism.<br /> <br /> That's also the reason for necrotech, the Silver Prince's doomfleet, the zombie plague, and the Dowager's well to alternate universes. They've got a denser concentration of sci-fi tropes than anything else in the Age of Sorrows.<br /> <br /> More generally, that's why all the 2E Deathlords had plans that would wreck Creation in a few years if your circle doesn't stop them in the near future. These were implemented derpily, and made the setting less fun. But they <i>did </i>evoke dread of the future, of death that can't be escaped no matter how much you do.<br /> <br /> The future's inevitable darkness is not the Abyssals' biggest theme. It's not their most important theme. But it's there, and it's worth keeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:28:11-07:00","id":88230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87696#post87696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'm starting a petition to Internet Congress that legally compels MrIsecure to post <i>at least</i> once per day.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T09:34:35-07:00","id":88234,"title":"","content":"Vampires are cool. Abyssals are like vampiric necromatic lords of death. Ergo, Abyssals are hella cool.<br /> <br /> Their link to Solars helps inform their place in the setting but is unnecessary to appreciate the concept of the splat. Really, this is true for all the Exalted types. They stand on their own and their relationship with others enriches them, but should not define them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T10:03:51-07:00","id":88257,"title":"","content":"To spin off what SurlySeraph said:<br /> <br /> The GSPs represent what the Solars became. The Abyssals represent what they could well have become, had the Prophecy of Darkness come to pass. Indeed, that's part of the reason the 3e Deathlords let Abyssals go independent - because after all, they know full well just how close the First Age Solars came to destroying the world. Repurpose the power of the Solars towards death, and, well...<br /> <br /> Naturally, the past we know seems a better match than the potential that might have been, because we know one happened and the other didn't. But in the Deathlords' minds - and in the minds of the eldest Sidereals, the ones who were there for the Great Prophecy - the Abyssals are the Solars' dark potential, returned to throw their shadow over the present day.<br /> <br /> The Abyssals are the ghosts of a future yet to come.<br /> <br /> It's one of our oldest myths, after all: the fate of the Sun is death. The Abyssals are that eventual fate, brought into the here and now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T10:47:06-07:00","id":88291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/87281-i-m-not-getting-abyssals?p=87696#post87696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssals represent the first sin, the Slaying of the Primordials during the Primordial War. Yeah, it was a great thing for the gods and humanity, but it was also a fundamentally selfish and destructive act that broke the very metaphysics of Creation. The Exalted are <i>murderers</i> dressed up in shiny clothing, <i>war criminals</i> bearing medals and honors that mock the victims of their atrocities. The Abyssal Exalted are the embodiments of this truth, the Solar Exaltation as it &quot;really&quot; is: black with sin, stained by the blood of the Primordials and an affront to all that is natural. They are the Exalted as the Neverborn see them, and guided by the Deathlords, the deathknights become the instruments of their vengeance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I would also like to say that, with the Reclamation gone, Infernals and Abyssals have a lot less overlap because Malfeas isn't coming to Creation. The Infernals are inclined to be the eccentric, decadent, sometimes wicked, sometimes righteous by their own standards, but always world-wrecking exemplars of what the Solars were in the first age. They exist to come to Creation and shove the heights and depths of both Hell and the First Age in everyone's faces. They are not just evil asshole Solars, because an evil asshole Solar can just be a Solar. Partial insanity is basically a condition of their Exaltation, like the risk of partial insanity is a condition of the Solar Exaltation.<br /> <br /> The Abyssals, on the other hand, are the Solars of another world. While the Solars might be the heroes Creation needs, the Abyssals might be the heroes the Underworld needs; Millions of ghosts, from the base peasant to the mighty Deathlord, have repeated the same patterns of behavior for centuries, rarely being able to resolve their problems and find what they are seeking, beholden to Creation while being locked out of it. Abyssals are the scions of the Underworld who can traverse the boundary. They can complete the projects of the dead and make Creation take the needs of this other world into account, this world whose very existence is disparaged by the Immaculate Faith. While Solars look to the future and try to change the world, the Abyssals are specially equipped to dispel old lies, discern the truth of the past, and end ancient grudges, either through peace or through exacting revenge. They are, almost literally, bridges between the living and the dead, and the number of sides they can potentially take in the coming conflict is nearly unfathomable. <br /> <br /> Whose past victims will be rallied to war against them by the Abyssals? Will it be the Realm, as Shadowlands containing all the victims of imperialism explode open across the Blessed Isle? Will it be the Elder Lunars whose forests are turned to ash and forced to turn over their dominion over the shadows? Perhaps even Heaven is brought to task when its crimes and failings are told and re-told through the words who died before they could speak of them. Maybe, one day, Saturn will be usurped by a new power who will usher in an era of reconciliation between the living and the dead. <br /> <br /> That is all up to the Abyssal PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1595-scatters-the-ashes","name":"Scatters-the-Ashes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}